## \ud83c\udfaf Lab Overview

**Learning Objectives:**
- Understand why tokens should be minted AFTER cooperative verification
- Implement custodial token model (cooperative owns tokens, farmer tracked off-chain)
- Integrate token minting with verification workflow
- Use verified quantity (not claimed quantity) for token minting
- Test end-to-end flow from batch creation through verification to tokenization

**What You'll Build:**
- \u2705 Post-verification token minting integrated with Telegram verification handler
- \u2705 `blockchain/token_manager.py` - Web3 wrapper for CoffeeBatchToken contract
- \u2705 Database integration with `token_id` column on `CoffeeBatch` table
- \u2705 Comprehensive integration test (`test_token_minting_flow.py`)
- \u2705 Enhanced smart contracts with `getTokenIdByBatchId()` function

**Prerequisites:**
- \u2705 Labs 1-12 completed (EPCIS events, verification system, aggregation)
- \u2705 Foundry installed and configured
- \u2705 Base Sepolia RPC access (Alchemy or similar)
- \u2705 Wallet with testnet ETH for deployment
- \u2705 PostgreSQL database with `CoffeeBatch` table
- \u2705 Telegram bot with verification system working

**Time Estimate:** 3-4 hours (implementation + testing + deployment)

**Cost:** ~$0.01 (Base Sepolia testnet deployment + testing)

